1
00:01:49,975 --> 00:01:53,655
I'm so sorry.
Can you help me? My tire...

2
00:01:53,815 --> 00:01:57,015
Sorry. I have an appointment.
I don't like to be late.

3
00:01:57,295 --> 00:01:59,856
Well, would you rather be late or dead?

4
00:02:01,615 --> 00:02:05,335
- You don't want to do this.
- Step out of the car.

5
00:02:11,976 --> 00:02:14,055
Whoo! Let's go, fellas!

6
00:02:14,256 --> 00:02:17,136
Come on, baby! Yes!

7
00:02:17,336 --> 00:02:19,536
Take it easy. The car's brand-new.

8
00:02:19,736 --> 00:02:24,616
- No problem, buddy. I got this.
- Baby, let's ride. Time to go.

9
00:02:24,896 --> 00:02:26,553
- Your parents know the kind of
company you're keeping?

10
00:02:26,555 --> 00:02:27,503
- Shut up.

11
00:02:29,296 --> 00:02:31,216
- This shit ain't working.
- It's coded.

12
00:02:31,417 --> 00:02:33,337
- What's the code?
- I can't give you that.

13
00:02:33,537 --> 00:02:36,616
We'll have to beat it out of you.
Get out the car.

14
00:02:36,897 --> 00:02:39,777
Come on, man. What you got for me?

15
00:02:39,976 --> 00:02:42,657
Kick your ass!

16
00:02:43,137 --> 00:02:45,137
Hold on.

17
00:02:45,337 --> 00:02:48,497
It just came out of the dry cleaner's.

18
00:03:07,778 --> 00:03:11,418
Hands up.
Stop moving or I will shoot you.

19
00:03:11,618 --> 00:03:14,098
Don't you have homework to do?

20
00:03:16,018 --> 00:03:19,378
- Why don't you go and do it?
- OK. I'm sorry.

21
00:03:23,298 --> 00:03:25,419
Late.

22
00:04:31,421 --> 00:04:33,701
Hey! Hey!

23
00:04:34,661 --> 00:04:38,982
- The game, the game, the game!
- What's the first rule when entering a man's car?

24
00:04:39,261 --> 00:04:42,901
- Respect a man's car, a man respects you.
- Rule number two.

25
00:04:43,101 --> 00:04:47,022
- Greet the man. Good afternoon, Frank.
- Good afternoon, Jack.

26
00:04:47,342 --> 00:04:50,862
- Can we play the game?
- I should think you'd be tired after school.

27
00:04:51,182 --> 00:04:54,702
- You're afraid I'm gonna win.
- You'll be too worn out to do your homework.

28
00:04:54,902 --> 00:04:58,662
- It's Friday. I don't have any homework.
- In that case, the game.

29
00:04:58,942 --> 00:05:03,262
- Yes!
- But first, what's the third rule of the car?

30
00:05:03,542 --> 00:05:04,862
Good.

31
00:05:20,503 --> 00:05:25,023
Five points. I'm white,
I'm round, but I'm not always around.

32
00:05:25,303 --> 00:05:28,103
- A tennis ball?
- Tennis balls are yellow.

33
00:05:40,943 --> 00:05:42,584
Four points.

34
00:05:42,743 --> 00:05:46,424
Sometimes I'm half, sometimes I'm whole.
Sometimes a slice of me is all you know.

35
00:05:46,583 --> 00:05:48,704
- A loaf of bread?
- No.

36
00:05:53,904 --> 00:05:57,705
Three points. Sometimes I'm light,
sometimes I'm dark. Sometimes I'm both.

37
00:05:57,904 --> 00:05:59,745
- I know. A light bulb.
- No.

38
00:05:59,944 --> 00:06:02,145
- A pizza!
- No.

39
00:07:01,307 --> 00:07:03,986
Audrey. Audrey! Stop walking away from me.

40
00:07:04,267 --> 00:07:07,267
Listen, we've got to finish this conversation.

41
00:07:09,747 --> 00:07:11,587
Where's he going?

42
00:07:14,947 --> 00:07:17,227
OK, look at me. Last clue for all the points.

43
00:07:17,427 --> 00:07:21,627
Everyone wants to walk on me,
but only a happy few ever have.

44
00:07:21,948 --> 00:07:23,947
Take your time.

45
00:07:31,988 --> 00:07:34,788
- Hey, bud.
- Shh! Mom, it's the game. I'm trying to think.

46
00:07:35,068 --> 00:07:38,508
- Sorry. Hey, Frank. How are you today?
- Well, Mrs. Billings.

47
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:42,068
- Can I team up with Mom?
- I don't know. It's not in the rules.

48
00:07:42,348 --> 00:07:45,709
Come on. What's the point in having rules
if you can't bend 'em?

49
00:07:45,908 --> 00:07:48,709
- OK. Just this once.
- Yeah!

50
00:07:48,988 --> 00:07:51,548
All right. Give me some clues.

51
00:07:51,748 --> 00:07:56,829
It's round, but not always around. It's light
sometimes, dark sometimes, or both.

52
00:07:57,109 --> 00:08:01,429
Everyone wants to walk on it,
but only a happy few ever have.

53
00:08:01,749 --> 00:08:05,069
- That is a hard one.
- Tell me about it.

54
00:08:08,269 --> 00:08:10,749
- The moon!
- Correct.

55
00:08:10,949 --> 00:08:13,029
Good job. All right. Come on.

56
00:08:13,229 --> 00:08:15,549
- See you Monday.
- Bye, Frank. Thanks.

57
00:08:15,749 --> 00:08:18,029
- Keep your snacks in the kitchen.
- Bye, Mom.

58
00:08:18,230 --> 00:08:21,110
He's really taken to you
in the month you've been with us.

59
00:08:21,310 --> 00:08:25,030
- Likewise.
- Too bad you can't stay on when Tony's back.

60
00:08:25,310 --> 00:08:28,390
It was just a favor.
I don't usually do this sort of a job.

61
00:08:28,670 --> 00:08:31,670
I thought you were a professional driver.

62
00:08:31,830 --> 00:08:33,750
A different kind of driving.

63
00:08:35,990 --> 00:08:39,910
Well, we're all gonna miss you
when you're gone.

64
00:08:46,431 --> 00:08:47,670
And...

65
00:08:47,871 --> 00:08:50,351
thank you for what you did.

66
00:08:50,550 --> 00:08:52,551
For what?

67
00:08:52,751 --> 00:08:56,791
For turning the car around so that
Jack wouldn't have to see us fighting.

68
00:08:57,071 --> 00:09:00,711
- You really know kids, don't you?
- I know fighting.

69
00:09:00,911 --> 00:09:03,311
He hasn't seen Jack in months,

70
00:09:03,511 --> 00:09:06,472
and when he gets back,
all I hear is what I'm doing wrong.

71
00:09:06,751 --> 00:09:12,031
You'd think that after being separated
for a year that he would...

72
00:09:13,392 --> 00:09:16,831
I'm sorry. You don't have to hear this.

73
00:09:17,032 --> 00:09:22,472
It's OK. For what it's worth,
I think you're doing a great job with Jack.

74
00:09:22,872 --> 00:09:24,112
Thank you.

75
00:09:24,232 --> 00:09:26,912
Any time I can be of help,
if there's anything you need.

76
00:09:27,072 --> 00:09:29,872
That's really sweet of you, Frank.

77
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:32,753
I might have to take you up on it.

78
00:09:35,513 --> 00:09:40,633
I almost forgot. I'm supposed to take Jack to
the doctor tomorrow morning for a checkup,

79
00:09:40,913 --> 00:09:45,313
but I'm organizing a party for him, even
though his birthday's not until next week.

80
00:09:48,113 --> 00:09:53,353
So, while I decorate and his friends arrive,
I was thinking, if you wouldn't mind...

81
00:09:53,753 --> 00:09:56,713
- I'll take him.
- I feel funny cutting into your weekend.

82
00:09:56,913 --> 00:09:59,874
I'm just picking up a friend at the airport
later on in the day.

83
00:10:00,193 --> 00:10:02,394
- That's nice.
- What is?

84
00:10:02,593 --> 00:10:05,553
The guys on security
say you're a bit of a loner. Um...

85
00:10:05,754 --> 00:10:10,154
- So it's just nice to hear you have a friend.
- He's not really a friend.

86
00:10:10,434 --> 00:10:12,554
He's French.

87
00:10:12,753 --> 00:10:15,314
I'll call you back.

88
00:10:15,514 --> 00:10:18,514
Audrey. I'd like to finish our conversation.

89
00:10:23,594 --> 00:10:26,354
If anything comes up before then,
you have my cell.

90
00:10:26,554 --> 00:10:30,475
- Nothing will come up, Mrs. Billings.
- Audrey.

91
00:10:30,754 --> 00:10:32,115
Audrey.

92
00:11:01,076 --> 00:11:03,875
- Yeah, hello?
- Confirmed for tomorrow. 9am.

93
00:11:50,477 --> 00:11:54,118
Tomorrow, 9am. Only change -
the driver'll be taking him, not the mother.

94
00:11:54,318 --> 00:11:55,558
Even better.

95
00:12:01,678 --> 00:12:04,478
Vasily?

96
00:12:14,078 --> 00:12:16,638
- Is it stable?
- Yes, it's stable.

97
00:12:16,758 --> 00:12:18,959
And the antidote?

98
00:12:26,438 --> 00:12:27,959
See you tomorrow.

99
00:12:39,199 --> 00:12:42,559
The drug-enforcement ministers
of six Latin American countries

100
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:44,839
arrived in Miami for a summit meeting...

101
00:12:45,039 --> 00:12:48,200
Yeah. Martin, Frank.
1156 Palmeadow.

102
00:12:48,399 --> 00:12:53,079
I'm waiting for an express delivery.
That's what you told me 45 minutes ago.

103
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:57,040
I don't need anything else.
Just get me the pizza.

104
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:59,800
- I'm not paying for that...
- Hi.

105
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:02,000
Hi.

106
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:07,400
So, it's one medium pie, no mozzarella,
extra olives and extra anchovies,

107
00:13:07,681 --> 00:13:09,800
which amounts to $11.95.

108
00:13:09,961 --> 00:13:12,481
- I hope you're hungry.
- You have no idea.

109
00:13:12,681 --> 00:13:15,721
I apologize for the delay, sir.

110
00:13:17,161 --> 00:13:19,081
Mrs. Billings.

111
00:13:20,921 --> 00:13:23,881
Audrey. Audrey.

112
00:13:24,641 --> 00:13:27,921
- What are you doing?
- What does it look like I'm doing?

113
00:13:28,121 --> 00:13:32,042
- Have you been drinking?
- A little.

114
00:13:33,962 --> 00:13:36,842
You said if I needed anything.

115
00:13:37,041 --> 00:13:40,841
- I can't.
- Why? Because of who I am?

116
00:13:42,122 --> 00:13:44,402
Because of who I am.

117
00:13:53,802 --> 00:13:57,442
I feel so lost. So confused.

118
00:13:58,803 --> 00:14:00,922
Who isn't?

119
00:14:10,482 --> 00:14:13,002
Thank you, Frank.

120
00:14:13,963 --> 00:14:16,523
For the time and...

121
00:14:16,723 --> 00:14:19,323
your respect.

122
00:14:19,523 --> 00:14:22,203
I think it's what I needed the most.

123
00:14:24,403 --> 00:14:26,123
Bye.

124
00:14:57,125 --> 00:14:59,885
- Am I gonna get a shot?
- I don't know.

125
00:15:21,765 --> 00:15:26,246
- Jeez. We're not open yet.
- I need to see the doctor immediately.

126
00:15:26,565 --> 00:15:30,566
Right. Dr. Koblin, if you'll come out here,
please. We have an issue.

127
00:15:30,885 --> 00:15:33,165
You'll have to state the medical problem.

128
00:15:33,366 --> 00:15:38,246
Actually, my problem's not medical.
It's psychological.

129
00:15:38,526 --> 00:15:40,926
Yes, Laura. What seems to be the problem?

130
00:15:41,126 --> 00:15:42,566
Me.

131
00:15:43,246 --> 00:15:45,526
I hate shots.

132
00:15:45,727 --> 00:15:49,286
Number one, there's no guarantee
you're getting a shot.

133
00:15:49,567 --> 00:15:53,326
There's no sense getting worked up
over something that might not happen.

134
00:15:59,446 --> 00:16:01,567
- Give me the news.
- Doctor said I'm cured.

135
00:16:02,407 --> 00:16:06,247
- Frank, it hurts a lot.
- I'd never let anyone hurt you a lot.

136
00:16:06,527 --> 00:16:09,247
- Promise?
- You know my fourth rule?

137
00:16:09,407 --> 00:16:13,367
Never make a promise
you can't keep. Come on.

138
00:16:15,447 --> 00:16:17,567
Close the door.

139
00:16:25,727 --> 00:16:26,968
Come on.

140
00:16:33,008 --> 00:16:35,888
- May I help you?
- Jack Billings to see Dr. Koblin.

141
00:16:36,088 --> 00:16:38,769
He's out sick today. He'll be seeing Dr. Tyberg.

142
00:16:39,048 --> 00:16:42,888
- I like Dr. Koblin.
- Don't worry. Dr. Tyberg's very nice.

143
00:16:43,089 --> 00:16:45,089
Just take him into room 3.

144
00:16:45,288 --> 00:16:46,929
- Where's Laura?
- Who?

145
00:16:47,129 --> 00:16:50,568
- You're standing at her desk.
- That Laura. She's out sick too.

146
00:16:50,849 --> 00:16:54,609
There's a lot of flu going around.
Now, come on. Doctor's got a busy day.

147
00:16:54,769 --> 00:16:57,769
Come on. It'll be over before you know it.

148
00:16:59,289 --> 00:17:01,129
Hey, hey!

149
00:17:01,889 --> 00:17:04,289
I'm Dr. Tyberg.

150
00:17:04,570 --> 00:17:06,490
Can't I wait for my doctor?

151
00:17:06,569 --> 00:17:09,569
Your doctor was called away
on an emergency.

152
00:17:09,850 --> 00:17:12,730
- The nurse said he had the flu.
- That was the emergency.

153
00:17:12,930 --> 00:17:18,970
He came down with flu, very quickly.
So, the sooner we start, the sooner we finish.

154
00:17:19,330 --> 00:17:22,490
Come. I show you something very cool.

155
00:17:22,690 --> 00:17:25,970
I'm sorry. Doctor-patient privacy in room.

156
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:29,330
You can wait in reception area,
or glass of water, or...

157
00:17:29,490 --> 00:17:33,450
Hey, trust me. I am doctor.

158
00:17:33,731 --> 00:17:35,730
Please. It's phone.

159
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:42,451
<i>- Yeah?
- Allô, allô.  Frank? I am here.</i>

160
00:17:42,731 --> 00:17:45,410
- You're early.
- Yeah, we had fantastic tailwinds.

161
00:17:45,611 --> 00:17:48,131
Put two hours on my vacation, just like that.

162
00:17:48,291 --> 00:17:51,851
From now on, it's the only way I'm flying.
Tailwinds or nothing.

163
00:17:52,131 --> 00:17:54,811
Glad you made it.

164
00:17:56,371 --> 00:18:01,171
Hello. Sorry, Dr. Dunietz is not in today.
Call back Monday.

165
00:18:06,732 --> 00:18:10,371
I'm a little tied up. You mind taking a cab?
You have the address, yes?

166
00:18:10,652 --> 00:18:16,212
Oh, thank you. I heard the fish down here
is fantastic. I could make us a bouillabaisse.

167
00:18:16,492 --> 00:18:19,012
You like bouillabaisse, Frank, no?

168
00:18:20,052 --> 00:18:22,252
I gotta go.

169
00:18:22,452 --> 00:18:23,492
Frank!

170
00:18:23,612 --> 00:18:26,092
Maybe we'll wait for his regular doctor.

171
00:18:26,293 --> 00:18:28,693
It's important that he receives immunizations.

172
00:18:28,972 --> 00:18:32,613
- I'm sure. But a week won't make a difference.
- No, we're doing it now.

173
00:18:54,093 --> 00:18:55,814
Get going, Jack!

174
00:20:03,736 --> 00:20:06,296
Look at me. Look at me.

175
00:20:06,496 --> 00:20:09,376
- Remember my promise?
- Yes.

176
00:20:29,337 --> 00:20:31,337
- It's... It's me!
- Get out!

177
00:20:35,657 --> 00:20:37,578
Frank.

178
00:21:05,978 --> 00:21:07,138
Shit.

179
00:21:15,739 --> 00:21:19,859
The patient's not cooperating.
Prep the vehicle.

180
00:21:32,900 --> 00:21:35,300
Come on, hurry.

181
00:21:38,980 --> 00:21:41,459
Don't worry. Everything's gonna be OK.

182
00:22:07,941 --> 00:22:11,661
- Freeze! Put your guns on the ground!
- Get down!

183
00:22:12,701 --> 00:22:15,221
<i>- Si.
- They got away.</i>

184
00:22:15,421 --> 00:22:17,021
<i>- Cazzo!
- Plan B?</i>

185
00:22:19,341 --> 00:22:20,301
Yes. Plan B.

186
00:22:38,622 --> 00:22:41,022
Oh, you made it.

187
00:22:41,222 --> 00:22:43,782
- Oh, what's that?
- Jack's birthday present.

188
00:22:43,982 --> 00:22:47,142
Baseball uniform, cleats, glove and a bat.

189
00:22:49,542 --> 00:22:53,183
- It's his favorite sport.
- It was. Last year.

190
00:22:53,382 --> 00:22:56,183
He's on a soccer team now. He's good.

191
00:22:56,462 --> 00:22:59,702
- You know, you should see him sometime.
- Hello.

192
00:22:59,903 --> 00:23:04,022
- Mr. And Mrs. Billings! They're coming!
- Hide, everyone. Hide!

193
00:23:11,303 --> 00:23:13,343
- Yes.
- Good morning, Mr. Driver.

194
00:23:13,543 --> 00:23:17,064
- Who is this?
- Look in your rear-view mirror and you'll see.

195
00:23:18,504 --> 00:23:21,024
I know what you're thinking.
Bulletproof glass.

196
00:23:21,103 --> 00:23:26,103
So tell me, in your experience - which judging
from the performance you put on in the office

197
00:23:26,384 --> 00:23:28,664
goes way beyond driving children to school -

198
00:23:28,983 --> 00:23:32,784
does bulletproof glass stop
a 7.62 armor-piercing round?

199
00:23:32,984 --> 00:23:36,264
Frank, why have you stopped the car?

200
00:23:39,024 --> 00:23:41,704
Don't look,
they are triangulated over 300 feet away.

201
00:23:41,904 --> 00:23:43,144
Frank, pick up.

202
00:23:43,345 --> 00:23:48,344
You screwed up my plan.
I am going to tell you how to set things right.

203
00:23:48,625 --> 00:23:52,065
Someone is going to appear in a few seconds.

204
00:24:03,305 --> 00:24:05,225
Let her in.

205
00:24:12,105 --> 00:24:14,625
Driver.

206
00:24:14,705 --> 00:24:17,866
Good boy. Good boy.

207
00:24:22,106 --> 00:24:23,266
Hi.

208
00:24:24,226 --> 00:24:26,146
Leave it on.

209
00:24:28,346 --> 00:24:32,746
Personally, I hate kids. I don't know
what your feelings are on the subject,

210
00:24:33,026 --> 00:24:38,226
but if you ever want to have any, make
no moves but the moves I tell you to make.

211
00:24:38,506 --> 00:24:43,026
You're in her hands now. They can be gentle
hands, but they can be the hands from hell.

212
00:24:43,306 --> 00:24:46,547
- Trust me on this one.
- Trust him on this one.

213
00:24:46,827 --> 00:24:48,666
Now, drive.

214
00:25:29,028 --> 00:25:30,948
Make a left.

215
00:25:31,148 --> 00:25:32,669
I said left.

216
00:25:53,029 --> 00:25:56,869
Listen, we keep doing this your way,
they're gonna catch us.

217
00:25:57,150 --> 00:25:59,829
- Do this my way, no one gets hurt.
- Where's the fun in that?

218
00:26:00,030 --> 00:26:02,509
Let's save the fun for later.

219
00:26:09,990 --> 00:26:11,070
Hey!

220
00:27:50,393 --> 00:27:51,474
Not bad.

221
00:27:51,673 --> 00:27:54,154
Didn't your mother
teach you to say thank you?

222
00:27:54,354 --> 00:27:56,274
She tried, and failed miserably.

223
00:27:56,434 --> 00:28:00,114
- I think we lost them.
- Think again.

224
00:28:04,514 --> 00:28:06,914
Thought complete. Let's go.

225
00:28:35,395 --> 00:28:40,275
You can't find him? He's one man in one car.
He's a chauffeur, for chrissakes.

226
00:28:40,555 --> 00:28:43,635
Not exactly, sir.
There's a possibility he was in on it.

227
00:28:43,915 --> 00:28:46,515
- That's impossible.
- How would you know?

228
00:28:46,716 --> 00:28:50,756
He could have been setting this up the
whole time, and you wouldn't have known.

229
00:28:51,036 --> 00:28:54,956
- And you are an expert on knowing people.
- His background.

230
00:28:56,116 --> 00:29:00,316
He's ex-Special Forces. Headed a commando
unit. Specialized in search and destroy.

231
00:29:00,596 --> 00:29:04,276
Been in and out of Lebanon, Syria, Sudan.
The man is a hunter.

232
00:29:04,556 --> 00:29:06,956
I don't care what his skills are
or where he's from.

233
00:29:07,156 --> 00:29:09,997
This is not a war zone,
this is an American city!

234
00:29:10,196 --> 00:29:12,316
Where's my son?

235
00:29:39,278 --> 00:29:41,558
Last stop. All out.

236
00:29:43,877 --> 00:29:48,078
You're quite a guy.
Another time, another place -

237
00:29:48,358 --> 00:29:52,038
you and me, baby,
the pleasure we could have.

238
00:29:57,678 --> 00:29:59,518
Beauty.

239
00:30:00,279 --> 00:30:02,758
Frank.

240
00:30:03,918 --> 00:30:04,878
Frank!

241
00:30:07,079 --> 00:30:08,118
Frank!

242
00:30:08,319 --> 00:30:13,199
Not what you expected when you reported
for work this morning, is it, Frank? No?

243
00:30:13,519 --> 00:30:16,399
Is that what passes for wit in this circle?

244
00:30:16,559 --> 00:30:20,119
In this circle, my friend,
wit is not a requirement of the job.

245
00:30:20,399 --> 00:30:23,959
Brutality, yes.
An ability to inflict pain, absolutely.

246
00:30:24,239 --> 00:30:29,599
A certain psychotic, moral ignorance,
blind obedience, all required.

247
00:30:29,920 --> 00:30:32,200
- But not wit. How was it?
- Fun.

248
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:35,200
Only the beginning, my love.

249
00:30:36,319 --> 00:30:39,200
- What's this all about?
- A timely question.

250
00:30:39,400 --> 00:30:41,320
Max.

251
00:30:41,520 --> 00:30:43,600
Pardon me.

252
00:30:51,281 --> 00:30:54,920
- Hello.
- Put me on the speaker.

253
00:30:55,241 --> 00:30:58,961
In the next two hours,
you'll get five million dollars in $100 bills.

254
00:30:59,240 --> 00:31:02,881
Put them in a waterproof suitcase,
go to the Bayfront Park - personally.

255
00:31:03,080 --> 00:31:07,201
There will be a blue Chrysler parked there.
Place the suitcase in the trunk, and leave.

256
00:31:07,481 --> 00:31:10,361
I don't know if I can get
five million dollars in two hours.

257
00:31:10,561 --> 00:31:14,321
I read the newspapers. When you were
appointed to your current position,

258
00:31:14,521 --> 00:31:18,321
your net worth exceeded 100 million dollars,
so you won't even feel the bite.

259
00:31:18,642 --> 00:31:21,882
What guarantee do I have
that you won't harm my son?

260
00:31:23,041 --> 00:31:25,922
"Guarantee"? Mr. Billings,
I am not a car dealer.

261
00:31:26,121 --> 00:31:29,841
Don't let the charming accent
and my impeccable syntax mislead you.

262
00:31:30,122 --> 00:31:33,602
I live in the jungle, and in the jungle
you either eat or be eaten.

263
00:31:33,762 --> 00:31:36,562
But, in the spirit of business,
here is the guarantee.

264
00:31:36,842 --> 00:31:40,282
Ten minutes past the deadline,
if the money doesn't arrive, I send a finger.

265
00:31:40,482 --> 00:31:44,042
20 minutes, a hand. 30 minutes, a foot.

266
00:31:44,323 --> 00:31:46,843
Sounds like we have a deal.

267
00:31:47,002 --> 00:31:49,322
You have a deal.

268
00:31:50,362 --> 00:31:52,963
Could we please speak to our son?

269
00:31:54,403 --> 00:31:56,403
Mommy! Mommy!

270
00:31:57,483 --> 00:32:01,483
You have two hours, Mr. Billings.
Starting now.

271
00:32:03,523 --> 00:32:06,883
- Just get my son!
- All right. All right.

272
00:32:07,163 --> 00:32:10,604
Frank, you promised
you wouldn't let anybody hurt me!

273
00:32:10,803 --> 00:32:14,843
- You promised!
- Never make promises you can't keep.

274
00:32:15,123 --> 00:32:18,284
I don't. It's one of my rules.

275
00:32:18,484 --> 00:32:19,804
Wow.

276
00:32:19,924 --> 00:32:25,684
Bravo. A man who leads his life by rules.
In my world rules are meant to be broken.

277
00:32:26,044 --> 00:32:30,284
- Not mine.
- You're gonna have to make an exception.

278
00:32:30,564 --> 00:32:32,484
Go.

279
00:32:59,805 --> 00:33:02,206
<i>Prego. </i>

280
00:33:13,126 --> 00:33:14,686
- Go.
- Hey, driver!

281
00:33:17,845 --> 00:33:22,846
No, no, wait, wait.
A little distance between us isn't a bad thing.

282
00:33:23,606 --> 00:33:25,526
<i>Andiamo!</i>

283
00:33:33,486 --> 00:33:35,687
Now.

284
00:34:08,688 --> 00:34:10,688
Hold on. The signal.

285
00:34:10,887 --> 00:34:13,288
- Hello.
- It's me.

286
00:34:13,448 --> 00:34:16,448
- You son of a bitch.
- Look, I had nothing to do with this.

287
00:34:16,728 --> 00:34:20,088
- One scratch on his head...
- Let me speak to who's in charge.

288
00:34:20,288 --> 00:34:23,809
- This is US Marshal Stappleton.
- Act fast. There are three boats.

289
00:34:24,128 --> 00:34:27,169
- Tell us where you are.
- Get a plane. They're heading north.

290
00:34:27,368 --> 00:34:30,248
- Tell me where you are.
- Just tell us where you are!

291
00:34:30,529 --> 00:34:32,248
Hello, Frank?

292
00:34:32,728 --> 00:34:34,849
Got it.

293
00:35:01,690 --> 00:35:04,090
<i>- Allô.
- Tarconi, it's me. Get out of the house.</i>

294
00:35:04,289 --> 00:35:08,210
- I was just putting the Madeleines...
- Forget the Madeleines, just get out.

295
00:35:08,530 --> 00:35:10,930
- And go where?
- Anywhere. Go to the beach.

296
00:35:11,090 --> 00:35:14,370
Oh, the beach. The famous Miami Beach.

297
00:35:14,650 --> 00:35:18,411
Oh, my dream.
I would love to go to the beach.

298
00:35:21,771 --> 00:35:23,370
Maybe not.

299
00:35:23,490 --> 00:35:26,850
- Freeze! Who the fuck are you?
- I'm the cook.

300
00:35:29,051 --> 00:35:32,211
Oh. This is a mistake. A terrible mistake.

301
00:35:34,331 --> 00:35:38,531
Why we can't all just get along, you know?

302
00:35:53,772 --> 00:35:57,732
- Hello.
- It's Frank. Pretend it's someone else.

303
00:36:00,132 --> 00:36:01,852
Hi, Susan.

304
00:36:02,412 --> 00:36:04,412
No, I'm just here at home.

305
00:36:04,612 --> 00:36:07,772
I didn't do it, Audrey.
She had a gun on Jack. I had no choice.

306
00:36:07,972 --> 00:36:12,212
Yeah, I saw that. What do you know?

307
00:36:12,492 --> 00:36:15,173
- It's more than a kidnapping.
- They asked for a ransom.

308
00:36:15,372 --> 00:36:21,133
The doctors, they were fake. They were trying
to give Jack a shot. When I interrupted them...

309
00:36:23,132 --> 00:36:27,733
I promised Jack I wouldn't let anyone
hurt him. I'm not gonna break that promise.

310
00:36:28,013 --> 00:36:30,053
- Frank.
- I'll call you back.

311
00:36:33,093 --> 00:36:35,214
Audrey.

312
00:36:35,413 --> 00:36:41,173
- Is everything all right?
- That's a pretty stupid question to ask, Jeff.

313
00:36:47,574 --> 00:36:51,213
All right. So tell me again, Inspector Tarconi,

314
00:36:51,534 --> 00:36:56,814
why you didn't immediately
identify yourself as a police officer.

315
00:36:57,094 --> 00:37:02,174
Oh, I was overwhelmed
by the effectiveness of your operation,

316
00:37:02,534 --> 00:37:04,654
the sophistication of your equipment.

317
00:37:04,855 --> 00:37:10,135
You know, I work in a small office
in a small town. We only have small crimes.

318
00:37:10,414 --> 00:37:14,055
- I must admit I was a little insecure.
- You and Frank Martin are friends, right?

319
00:37:14,335 --> 00:37:19,895
A friend? Oh, I wouldn't say exactly a friend.
I know him, we have a relationship.

320
00:37:20,215 --> 00:37:22,135
A long relationship?

321
00:37:22,295 --> 00:37:24,895
- Not so long.
- But they found you cooking in his house.

322
00:37:25,095 --> 00:37:26,335
- I'm French!
- So?

323
00:37:26,535 --> 00:37:31,215
We don't need to know someone for long time in
order to cook for them. It's our way of breaking the ice.

324
00:37:31,496 --> 00:37:36,135
Take, for example, this sandwich
and coffee you so graciously offer me.

325
00:37:36,416 --> 00:37:39,455
Well, pardon me to think so,
but it's not very good.

326
00:37:39,656 --> 00:37:42,256
I know it sucks, but what's that
got to do with anything?

327
00:37:42,536 --> 00:37:43,616
Do you have a kitchen?

328
00:37:46,016 --> 00:37:47,896
Stay back. Stay back.

329
00:39:10,099 --> 00:39:12,779
Don't move. Smith!

330
00:39:12,899 --> 00:39:14,819
Drop it.

331
00:39:39,740 --> 00:39:42,220
Oh, Jesus. What happened?

332
00:39:42,421 --> 00:39:45,500
We'll take care of it for you.

333
00:39:51,340 --> 00:39:54,021
- Are you sure this safe?
- Look over your shoulder.

334
00:39:54,220 --> 00:39:56,620
We got you covered.

335
00:40:05,141 --> 00:40:11,661
As my mother used to say,
a meal is only limited by your imagination.

336
00:40:12,062 --> 00:40:14,462
<i>- Crème brûlée et croque monsieur.
- Cream brûlée?</i>

337
00:40:14,661 --> 00:40:15,821
- Crème brûlée.
- Cock?

338
00:40:15,981 --> 00:40:18,502
- Croque monsieur.
- Croque monsieur.

339
00:40:20,021 --> 00:40:21,862
<i>- Oui?
- Where are you?</i>

340
00:40:22,022 --> 00:40:25,102
- Cooking.
- Cooking. Can you talk?

341
00:40:25,302 --> 00:40:28,382
- Oh, speak of the devil. My mother.
- Mom.

342
00:40:28,542 --> 00:40:31,622
Please, do you mind?

343
00:40:31,902 --> 00:40:33,262
Thank you.

344
00:40:33,342 --> 00:40:35,262
<i>Oui, Maman. Je suis très bien arrivé. </i>

345
00:40:35,463 --> 00:40:39,222
<i>Oui, très très bien, merci. Oui.
Ah, oui, c'est une très jolie ville. </i>

346
00:40:39,502 --> 00:40:43,143
- May I ask who you're cooking for?
- For the US marshals.

347
00:40:43,422 --> 00:40:48,623
Once they found my badge, they were very
polite. They gave me a coffee and a sandwich.

348
00:40:48,903 --> 00:40:51,383
You wouldn't believe what passes
for food in this place, Frank.

349
00:40:51,582 --> 00:40:56,663
I am correcting the situation while they wait
for my chief to call back and confirm everything.

350
00:40:57,063 --> 00:41:01,543
Of course, that might take a while.
He's never there.

351
00:41:01,744 --> 00:41:04,903
- Anything about me?
- They are very interested about you.

352
00:41:05,104 --> 00:41:08,743
They want to know where you are.
Where are you?

353
00:41:09,023 --> 00:41:12,024
Nowhere for very long. Listen, hold on.

354
00:41:15,823 --> 00:41:18,544
Do you have access to a computer?

355
00:41:18,704 --> 00:41:22,184
Easier than having access
to something decent to eat.

356
00:41:36,865 --> 00:41:41,144
- Oh, handsome fellow. Who is he?
- That's what I need to know. Do they have an ID program?

357
00:41:41,345 --> 00:41:46,905
Forgive me. I'm not so used to this system.
Back home, there is one computer for ten of us.

358
00:41:47,305 --> 00:41:49,505
So, how is it with you, Frank?

359
00:41:49,705 --> 00:41:52,945
- It's a complicated story.
- Ah, you mean you are in the shit?

360
00:41:53,265 --> 00:41:56,985
- You might say that.
- In other words, your natural state.

361
00:41:57,186 --> 00:41:58,626
Voilà.

362
00:41:58,705 --> 00:42:04,946
A Russian biologist with advanced degrees from
the state laboratory for biological warfare in Siberia.

363
00:42:05,346 --> 00:42:10,706
- Do we have an address?
- Miami, Boca West, King Street, number 11.

364
00:43:49,950 --> 00:43:51,589
Get out!

365
00:44:16,631 --> 00:44:18,271
Hey!

366
00:44:21,791 --> 00:44:25,351
- What are you doing?
- Trying to catch a bus.

367
00:44:27,551 --> 00:44:29,271
Come on.

368
00:44:44,432 --> 00:44:48,752
What are you doing, driver?
Not so good on the water, hey?

369
00:44:52,112 --> 00:44:53,472
Stop it! Stop it!

370
00:45:23,273 --> 00:45:25,953
- OK. OK.
- Tell me about the doctor's office.

371
00:45:26,073 --> 00:45:29,313
- What doctor's office?
- Where you tried to stick the kid with this.

372
00:45:29,633 --> 00:45:31,634
You want to tell me?

373
00:45:40,834 --> 00:45:43,994
Do you know what you have done?
Do you know what you have done?

374
00:45:44,194 --> 00:45:48,994
Obviously something not conducive to your good health,
which is all I needed to know in the first place.

375
00:45:49,274 --> 00:45:51,674
Have a good life...

376
00:45:51,874 --> 00:45:53,994
what's left of it.

377
00:46:08,274 --> 00:46:12,595
- Outpost to base. The ransom is still there.
- Thanks.

378
00:46:12,875 --> 00:46:14,675
The ransom hasn't been picked up.

379
00:46:14,875 --> 00:46:17,955
- Don't worry.
- What if it's not just a kidnapping?

380
00:46:18,235 --> 00:46:22,555
- I've worked on many kidnapping cases.
- If they don't take it I won't get my son back.

381
00:46:22,756 --> 00:46:25,516
Don't make this
any more complicated than it is.

382
00:46:25,835 --> 00:46:29,555
I'm not making this complicated, Jefferson.
It's because of your job.

383
00:46:29,635 --> 00:46:33,316
- What does my job have to do with this?
- It has everything to do with it.

384
00:46:33,595 --> 00:46:36,756
Because you became famous,
we became the targets.

385
00:46:37,036 --> 00:46:42,396
No matter what you think, the only one who's
out there trying to get Jack back is Frank.

386
00:46:42,676 --> 00:46:45,076
- The chauffeur?
- You spoke to Frank Martin?

387
00:46:45,276 --> 00:46:50,556
- What the hell are you doing talking to him?
- Because he's the last person who saw Jack alive!

388
00:46:50,837 --> 00:46:52,556
We've found the boy.

389
00:47:17,797 --> 00:47:19,237
Hard drive blew.

390
00:47:19,317 --> 00:47:21,237
- Get another one in there.
- Yes, sir.

391
00:47:21,357 --> 00:47:24,717
- How long is it gonna take?
- Ma'am, we're going as fast as we can.

392
00:47:24,998 --> 00:47:27,278
- He can suffocate in there.
- Stay calm.

393
00:47:27,477 --> 00:47:29,397
- It's my son!
- Let them work.

394
00:47:29,598 --> 00:47:32,358
- Are you gonna sit and do nothing?
- They're experts.

395
00:47:32,558 --> 00:47:36,118
Everyone is an expert!
I've had it with all of you!

396
00:47:36,398 --> 00:47:37,758
Audrey!

397
00:47:41,119 --> 00:47:43,318
Audrey!

398
00:47:43,598 --> 00:47:45,118
Audrey!

399
00:47:49,719 --> 00:47:51,159
Audrey!

400
00:47:53,479 --> 00:47:55,678
Mommy!

401
00:47:58,078 --> 00:48:00,079
Jack!

402
00:48:00,759 --> 00:48:02,879
Are you OK?

403
00:48:07,679 --> 00:48:10,359
There you go, little buddy.

404
00:48:14,480 --> 00:48:17,360
Breathe. Come on, breathe.

405
00:48:17,560 --> 00:48:20,800
- You're the devil.
- I wish.

406
00:48:57,241 --> 00:49:01,762
- Shit! Dimitri, you scare shit in me.
- Where is Sonovitch?

407
00:49:02,041 --> 00:49:04,841
- In chamber.
- I need to speak with him.

408
00:49:05,122 --> 00:49:08,962
Sit down! Listen Panasonic.
Is rap music, is good.

409
00:50:45,045 --> 00:50:46,605
- What was that?
- I don't know.

410
00:50:47,925 --> 00:50:49,485
Shit!

411
00:50:49,565 --> 00:50:51,566
- What are you doing?
- I need antidote.

412
00:50:51,765 --> 00:50:54,645
The driver, he inject me with virus. Look!

413
00:50:54,926 --> 00:50:58,966
- Dimitri, where would he get the virus?
- The one we left in doctor's surgery.

414
00:50:59,045 --> 00:51:01,846
Please, I need antidote. I am sick.

415
00:51:02,126 --> 00:51:05,966
Calm down. You're not sick. You have
four hours before the virus is active.

416
00:51:06,166 --> 00:51:08,366
You know that. You worked on creating it.

417
00:51:09,606 --> 00:51:11,806
- Open fridge.
- I'm telling you...

418
00:51:13,366 --> 00:51:17,487
<i>Izvinite.  Open fridge. Open the fridge!</i>

419
00:51:18,447 --> 00:51:21,807
Yes. Insurance policy. How many you have?

420
00:51:21,966 --> 00:51:25,127
Two doses. Enough for Tipov and myself.

421
00:51:28,206 --> 00:51:31,847
Tipov's policy cancelled. There is one for me.

422
00:51:32,047 --> 00:51:34,167
And I want it now. Come on.

423
00:51:34,367 --> 00:51:37,047
Come on. Let's do it!

424
00:51:39,607 --> 00:51:40,967
- Let's not.
- Who are you?

425
00:51:41,047 --> 00:51:43,087
- There is enough for two.
- You don't need it.

426
00:51:43,288 --> 00:51:45,767
- But you injected me.
- With water.

427
00:51:45,967 --> 00:51:48,448
- I'm not sick.
- You're not sick.

428
00:51:48,647 --> 00:51:50,287
- Water.
- Water.

429
00:51:52,087 --> 00:51:53,248
Son of bitch!

430
00:51:58,001 --> 00:52:01,201
Good. Our problem is solved.
One dose for each of us.

431
00:51:59,848 --> 00:52:02,227
- It's not for us.

432
00:52:02,550 --> 00:52:06,152
- One for you and one for the child.
_ Your devotion is touching.

433
00:52:06,361 --> 00:52:07,962
My patience is about to run out.

434
00:52:15,022 --> 00:52:18,302
- Tell me about the virus.
- OK. What do you want know?

435
00:52:18,582 --> 00:52:20,102
Everything. For starters, what is it?

436
00:52:20,102 --> 00:52:23,383
A recombinant retro-immune
double-polymorphing effluent.

437
00:52:23,662 --> 00:52:27,703
The child will die. Anyone he breathes
on will die, and then it's over.

438
00:52:27,982 --> 00:52:32,182
- What do you mean, "It's over?"
- The virus is designed to go inert after 24 hours.

439
00:52:32,503 --> 00:52:36,142
Thanks for the lesson.
Now give me the vials.

440
00:52:36,343 --> 00:52:41,583
You really want to play superhero, don't you?
Well, let's see if you can fly.

441
00:53:16,704 --> 00:53:18,904
- You OK?
- I'm OK.

442
00:54:20,947 --> 00:54:25,946
There's nothing to worry about. It's just a simple viral
infection combined with the stress of what happened.

443
00:54:26,147 --> 00:54:29,707
It should pass in a day or two.
I gave him something to help him sleep.

444
00:54:29,987 --> 00:54:34,107
- Call me if anything arises.
- Thank you, Doctor.

445
00:54:35,748 --> 00:54:39,267
You know, Audrey, all this has...

446
00:54:39,547 --> 00:54:43,107
well, it's made me realize
what a fool I've been.

447
00:54:43,308 --> 00:54:45,507
With Jack...

448
00:54:45,708 --> 00:54:48,188
and with you.

449
00:54:50,588 --> 00:54:55,308
- Are you OK?
- Mr. Billings. We're running late.

450
00:54:55,588 --> 00:55:00,588
I'll be right out.
I'd like to come by after the conference,

451
00:55:00,748 --> 00:55:03,428
check on Jack.

452
00:55:03,628 --> 00:55:05,749
Check on you.

453
00:55:07,669 --> 00:55:10,909
Good. I'll see you soon.

454
00:55:11,109 --> 00:55:13,309
They're here if you need them.

455
00:55:24,949 --> 00:55:28,189
- Are you all right, ma'am?
- I'm fine.

456
00:55:31,550 --> 00:55:34,430
- Hello.
- It's me.

457
00:55:34,509 --> 00:55:36,350
- Are you OK?
- Go to your bedroom.

458
00:55:36,549 --> 00:55:39,430
Hi, Susan. How are you?

459
00:55:41,150 --> 00:55:44,110
I'm alone. Where are you, Frank?

460
00:55:44,309 --> 00:55:46,430
Turn around.

461
00:55:56,590 --> 00:55:59,950
Frank, you were wrong.
It was a kidnapping. Jack is fine.

462
00:56:00,111 --> 00:56:05,111
Jack's been infected with a virus. Anyone
who comes into contact with him will die.

463
00:56:05,391 --> 00:56:07,710
What are you telling me?

464
00:56:07,911 --> 00:56:12,231
- Are you telling me my son is gonna die?
- No, he's not.

465
00:56:14,431 --> 00:56:18,551
Once incubated, the virus becomes airborne,
so anyone he breathes on gets infected.

466
00:56:18,751 --> 00:56:21,431
Your son was a weapon.
The target is his father.

467
00:56:21,631 --> 00:56:26,311
- Jefferson? Well, why?
- Because of the conference. It's the only logical answer.

468
00:56:26,591 --> 00:56:29,591
Every drug-enforcement agency
in the hemisphere, in one room.

469
00:56:29,872 --> 00:56:32,752
Your husband breathes, the room dies.

470
00:56:38,472 --> 00:56:40,992
You gotta trust me, Audrey.

471
00:56:47,872 --> 00:56:50,192
Can you get to him?

472
00:56:50,472 --> 00:56:53,273
- What are you gonna do?
- Find the guy responsible.

473
00:56:53,472 --> 00:56:56,633
He has more of this.
For you and everybody else.

474
00:56:58,553 --> 00:57:00,752
For you now.

475
00:57:16,554 --> 00:57:17,514
We have a guest.

476
00:57:19,353 --> 00:57:22,434
- You're burning up.
- I'm OK.

477
00:57:22,593 --> 00:57:24,834
You gotta go. Go.

478
00:57:28,154 --> 00:57:29,433
Don't move!

479
00:58:12,675 --> 00:58:14,795
- Is the governor here?
- Everybody's gonna be here.

480
00:58:14,955 --> 00:58:18,035
The govenor, delegates
from all over the world.

481
00:58:18,155 --> 00:58:21,515
- Just a second. Hello.
- Jefferson, you can't go to the conference.

482
00:58:21,676 --> 00:58:24,836
- Is everything all right?
... to give him a deadly virus...

483
00:58:25,156 --> 00:58:28,116
- Audrey, I can't hear you. I'm inside.
- Now I've got it, and so do you.

484
00:58:28,316 --> 00:58:31,676
- Audrey, I can't hear you.
- Their plan is to infect everyone at the conference.

485
00:58:31,956 --> 00:58:34,636
- I'm gonna have to call you back.
- Jeff!

486
00:58:36,636 --> 00:58:39,717
Mr. Billings, are you all right?

487
00:58:39,916 --> 00:58:43,077
- I'm all right. Come on, let's go.
- You sure?

488
00:59:02,717 --> 00:59:05,717
<i>- Allô.
- You still a guest of the government?</i>

489
00:59:05,917 --> 00:59:10,678
They gave me the five-star accommodation.
Let me guess - you need my help.

490
00:59:11,077 --> 00:59:13,398
Are you near the computer?

491
00:59:13,558 --> 00:59:16,758
It's practically my pillow.
So, how do you want to start?

492
00:59:16,918 --> 00:59:23,078
- I don't know. I have nothing.
- Ah. My favorite type of investigation.

493
00:59:23,438 --> 00:59:26,238
<i>Let's see. Alors. </i>

494
00:59:26,918 --> 00:59:29,958
I'd like to take this opportunity
to introduce you to my delegates...

495
00:59:30,278 --> 00:59:34,559
Breathe. That's right,
breathe, my friend, breathe.

496
00:59:34,878 --> 00:59:37,919
Tomorrow, once these
bastards are out of the way

497
00:59:38,119 --> 00:59:42,839
and their co-operation agreements are dead and buried,
you know what the biggest problem is going to be?

498
00:59:43,118 --> 00:59:45,799
- What?
- Counting the money.

499
00:59:50,319 --> 00:59:52,799
- I can't wait for tomorrow.
- Ay-ay-ay!

500
00:59:57,039 --> 01:00:00,079
Aah. Gianni Chellini.

501
01:00:00,360 --> 01:00:04,880
Hires himself out to anyone looking to make
trouble like the Red Brigade, Shining Path.

502
01:00:06,999 --> 01:00:10,359
Someone accessed a database
on the 15th floor.

503
01:00:10,640 --> 01:00:14,480
That's Gonzalez. He's on vacation.

504
01:00:14,760 --> 01:00:19,280
Was behind the hostage-taking
of the OPEC ministers in Geneva.

505
01:00:19,560 --> 01:00:21,840
It was a nice piece of work.

506
01:00:26,161 --> 01:00:28,280
- Give me an address.
- Miami, East Highland,

507
01:00:28,480 --> 01:00:30,601
Pelican Drive, number 26900.

508
01:00:30,681 --> 01:00:33,561
- We've found the car.
- You're one great cop, Tarconi.

509
01:00:33,760 --> 01:00:37,480
Thank you for the compliment.
Now I'm going back to sleep.

510
01:00:40,841 --> 01:00:42,561
Hm. Maybe not.

511
01:00:44,881 --> 01:00:47,841
- Bumbaclaat, man! Move out the way!
- Move over.

512
01:00:48,041 --> 01:00:50,042
I'll do ya!

513
01:00:57,842 --> 01:00:59,762
Mommy.

514
01:01:00,881 --> 01:01:05,122
- Honey. You feeling better?
- A little bit.

515
01:01:05,402 --> 01:01:08,562
Why don't you try to go back to sleep, OK?

516
01:01:14,122 --> 01:01:16,323
Ma'am, are you all right?

517
01:01:26,123 --> 01:01:28,523
Jefferson. Jefferson, are you OK?

518
01:02:30,645 --> 01:02:32,765
OK, do it.

519
01:02:44,766 --> 01:02:48,606
- What are you doing?
- You know, last night got me thinking.

520
01:02:48,806 --> 01:02:51,206
How do we transport the antidote safely?

521
01:02:51,486 --> 01:02:54,726
We need something that won't break.
Something that can't be stolen.

522
01:02:54,926 --> 01:02:58,686
Something totally secure. Me.

523
01:03:04,526 --> 01:03:07,606
Impressive. Get dressed.

524
01:03:09,326 --> 01:03:10,287
Stop him.

525
01:03:13,327 --> 01:03:15,646
- These your friends?
- Not yet.

526
01:03:25,047 --> 01:03:27,527
- Where'd they go?
- The garage.

527
01:03:29,087 --> 01:03:30,807
- I'm out of ammo.
- Me too.

528
01:03:30,887 --> 01:03:32,927
- So am I.
- Where are the reloads?

529
01:03:33,087 --> 01:03:34,527
The garage.

530
01:03:35,888 --> 01:03:38,368
Check the house. Go, go, go!

531
01:03:42,208 --> 01:03:44,128
Get him! Get him!

532
01:05:33,147 --> 01:05:36,226
- What d'you want me to do?
- Keep the meter running.

533
01:05:36,507 --> 01:05:41,427
Bye. Don't worry, baby.
You're safe now. You're safe.

534
01:05:41,706 --> 01:05:45,426
You're so beautiful.
Remind me of my yellow poom-poom rider.

535
01:06:58,909 --> 01:07:00,710
Don't move.

536
01:07:00,830 --> 01:07:03,789
- Oh, Mr. Driver.
- I'll blow you into tomorrow.

537
01:07:03,990 --> 01:07:07,629
But then I'll bleed what you came for all over
the floor. You wouldn't want this, would you?

538
01:07:07,910 --> 01:07:11,350
Not after you worked so hard
trying to get to the antidote.

539
01:07:11,550 --> 01:07:13,950
Take a good look, Frank Martin.

540
01:07:14,150 --> 01:07:17,510
I'm a cure for what ails you.
I'm the only cure for what ails you.

541
01:07:17,791 --> 01:07:20,750
I am the antidote.

542
01:07:20,950 --> 01:07:24,031
But nice try. I'm impressed.
I didn't give you enough credit.

543
01:07:24,310 --> 01:07:28,150
- It took more than a driver to figure this out.
- I haven't figured it all out yet.

544
01:07:28,351 --> 01:07:31,510
Perhaps I can help you.
What part are you a little thick on?

545
01:07:31,791 --> 01:07:34,871
- You. Why?
- Oh.

546
01:07:35,071 --> 01:07:40,711
That's the easy part. It's a business deal, pure
and simple. I'm for hire to the highest bidder.

547
01:07:41,111 --> 01:07:44,351
In this case, the highest bidder
was the Colombian cocaine cartels

548
01:07:44,552 --> 01:07:47,711
that wanted these pesky lawmen
off their backs.

549
01:07:47,991 --> 01:07:51,152
You really think killing all these politicians
is going to make things easier for them?

550
01:07:51,351 --> 01:07:54,512
That's not my problem.
I was hired to do a job.

551
01:07:54,832 --> 01:07:59,111
I did the job, like you. Just my pay is better.

552
01:08:00,392 --> 01:08:02,952
My hair and my suit, too.

553
01:08:04,592 --> 01:08:06,912
Oh, Lola.

554
01:08:07,072 --> 01:08:10,352
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I have a plane to catch.

555
01:08:11,392 --> 01:08:13,632
Kill him.

556
01:08:13,792 --> 01:08:15,432
<i>Ciao, ciao. </i>

557
01:08:19,192 --> 01:08:21,473
- Don't even blink.
- What's in this for you?

558
01:08:21,672 --> 01:08:23,592
Pleasure...

559
01:08:25,992 --> 01:08:28,753
in killing you.

560
01:10:00,757 --> 01:10:03,236
We're coming to you live
from the Key Biscayne causeway

561
01:10:03,517 --> 01:10:07,357
where at least ten police cars are in
hot pursuit of a stolen red pick-up truck.

562
01:10:11,677 --> 01:10:14,637
Oh, my. This is just nuts.
Jim, are you getting that?

563
01:10:14,837 --> 01:10:19,237
There's another car that is swaying
past the police, as if they were standing still.

564
01:10:19,557 --> 01:10:23,077
- Son of a bitch can drive. Whoo.
- Yes, he can.

565
01:11:07,799 --> 01:11:09,879
We have clearance for takeoff.

566
01:11:09,999 --> 01:11:14,799
Sit back, enjoy your flight, and
we will be in Colombia before you know it.

567
01:11:57,361 --> 01:12:00,241
We have a problem with the landing gear.
I need to land.

568
01:12:00,320 --> 01:12:02,641
- Can we fly with the problem?
- Theoretically.

569
01:12:02,841 --> 01:12:06,361
Then you'll land when we get to Colombia.

570
01:12:06,681 --> 01:12:09,161
Go and see if you can lift it manually.

571
01:12:09,361 --> 01:12:12,601
Sorry for the inconvenience.
Nothing to worry about.

572
01:12:17,202 --> 01:12:20,001
Sorry, flight's been cancelled.

573
01:12:20,202 --> 01:12:23,562
I'm sorry to inform you
that you have been cancelled.

574
01:12:23,721 --> 01:12:26,601
Have a seat.

575
01:12:27,282 --> 01:12:29,802
Relax.

576
01:12:29,962 --> 01:12:32,842
Drink something.
Let's get to know each other.

577
01:12:32,962 --> 01:12:36,202
I think I know everything I need to know.

578
01:14:20,071 --> 01:14:21,991
Shit.

579
01:15:57,435 --> 01:16:01,635
Five points. What has eyes
but no ears, skin but no hair,

580
01:16:01,835 --> 01:16:03,635
it's white inside and brown outside?

581
01:16:03,836 --> 01:16:05,675
- Mom?
- A worm?

582
01:16:05,876 --> 01:16:09,315
- Wrong. Dad?
- A caterpillar.

583
01:16:09,596 --> 01:16:12,275
- Wrong.
- A potato.

584
01:16:16,196 --> 01:16:19,196
- May I help you?
- I was just leaving.

585
01:16:22,556 --> 01:16:24,476
- Coconut.
- Wrong.

586
01:16:24,636 --> 01:16:27,996
- A snake.
- Wrong.

587
01:16:28,316 --> 01:16:31,276
- A peanut.
- Yuck!

588
01:16:31,476 --> 01:16:33,556
- A hot dog.
- Wrong.

589
01:16:46,037 --> 01:16:48,157
- That was fast.
- Yeah.

590
01:16:49,397 --> 01:16:54,477
- Didn't want you to miss your plane.
- That's very thoughtful of you.

591
01:17:02,237 --> 01:17:04,438
Check it out, my man.

592
01:17:06,757 --> 01:17:10,398
You won't believe
what happened to me last night.

593
01:17:15,878 --> 01:17:19,118
I have something for you.
Since you never got to the beach.

594
01:17:19,438 --> 01:17:24,398
Oh, you know, water's water, sand is sand.
Here, there - it's all the same.

595
01:17:24,678 --> 01:17:26,718
Flight 069 to Paris.

596
01:17:26,918 --> 01:17:29,678
Thank you, Frank.
It was an interesting vacation.

597
01:17:29,879 --> 01:17:32,959
- What more could one ask for?
- Ah, yeah.

598
01:17:33,998 --> 01:17:37,559
<i>- Au revoir, Frank.
- Au revoir, my friend. Have a good flight.</i>

599
01:17:37,718 --> 01:17:40,039
I doubt it. They said it is all headwinds.

600
01:17:40,239 --> 01:17:43,879
I guess we can't have
everything we wish for, can we?

601
01:17:44,639 --> 01:17:46,839
No, we can't.

602
01:18:01,119 --> 01:18:02,280
Yeah.

603
01:18:02,480 --> 01:18:05,160
I'm looking for a transporter.

604
01:18:08,600 --> 01:18:10,240
I'm listening.
